description:
Set sail from the port of Los Gigantes and go in search of the whales and dolphins that inhabit the coasts of Tenerife.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
After having photographed these amazing sea creatures you will sail near the cliffs of Masca and Los Gigantes.&nbsp; Reaching to a height of almost 600 metres, these cliffs are among the highest sea cliffs in Europe.
&nbsp;
During the tour, all drinks are included: red wine, beer, soft drinks and water. It also includes an on-board guide who will explain everything in your own language.


On your journey you will be accompanied by an &quot;Official whale observation guide&quot;. Do not forget your camera and swimsuit to take a swim!

Discover the magic of whale watching off the south coast of Tenerife aboard this exclusive sailboat.

With a length of 15.62 metres and a beam of 4.90 metres, this spacious and stable sailboat offers an unrivalled experience for those looking to enjoy the sun, the sea breeze and the breathtaking views of the island.

You&#39;ll be able to observe whales and dolphins up close in their natural habitat. And with room to comfortably accommodate 11 people in its six double cabins and three full bathrooms, it is ideal for family trips or trips with friends, whether on a guided excursion or a private charter.&nbsp;

Neptuno is a pleasure boat on which you can cruise along the south coast of Tenerife, swim in the ocean and even spot the whales and dolphins that inhabit the coast of the island.

&nbsp;

It has a maximum capacity of 22 passengers, so it is ideal if you want to enjoy an excursion in small groups.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Don&#39;t forget to bring sun cream, sunglasses and camera!

Bahriyeli offers a unique whale and dolphin watching experience in Tenerife in collaboration with Captain Paul Watson/Neptune&#39;s Pirates Foundation. During the two-hour tour, participants will be able to enjoy the south coast of Tenerife and observe various marine species in their natural habitat, including whales, dolphins, turtles and seabirds. This is a boat that prioritises animal welfare by maintaining a safe and respectful distance, allowing natural interactions without causing discomfort to the animals. Experienced guides will provide you with detailed information about the behaviour and characteristics of marine life, enriching the experience.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Through these excursions, they seek to raise awareness about the importance of preserving marine ecosystems and promote sustainable tourism practices. Participants have the opportunity to join this cause while enjoying the beauty of the ocean and contributing to the protection of marine species for future generations. In addition, Bahriyeli offers an educational experience on board, where expert crew provide information about the species sighted, the challenges faced by whales and dolphins around the world, including the Faroe Islands and the hunt in Taiji, and facts about captivity.

Share a pleasant moment with friends or family on one of the most exclusive and luxurious boats in the Canary Islands. With its 20-metre length, Opera 60 is one of the largest semi-rigid inflatable boats in the world.

Departing from Puerto Colon, the boat will take you along the coast of the south of Tenerife on a trip where you can dive into the crystal clear waters of the Atlantic and relax in the sun in search of whales and dolphins in their natural habitat. We will travel along the coast of Adeje until we reach La Caleta, where we will anchor for you to enjoy a swim in the sea before heading back to the port.&nbsp;

A qualified marine guide will accompany you throughout the trip to explain everything you need to know about the marine ecosystem and the incredible biodiversity of the south coast of Tenerife.

Amazing and unique sailing experience, that will delight everyone!

During the trip you can sail, swim or just relax. Their professional skippers will lead you along the beautiful coast of Tenerife. Otherwise the south-west coast of Tenerife&nbsp;
is a perfect place for whales and dolphins watching in their natural habitat.
Their boats have the &quot;Blue Flag&quot;, complying with applicable international regulations and ensure that the activity is carried out with the best respect, safety and responsibility.&nbsp;

You can share this experience with a small group of people or make the most exclusive charter with your family or friends.

We will leave from Puerto Colón to begin this unforgettable journey. Relax on our comfortable flybridge while you sip a refreshing drink and enjoy our menu. You can also take advantage of the paddle surf boards and snorkelling equipment we provide to dive into the waters of the Atlantic Ocean.

During the trip, we will anchor in one of the bays so that you can enjoy the spectacular view and the tranquillity of this environment before returning to the port.&nbsp;This boat is perfect for your private getaways, as it is rented on an exclusive basis.

&nbsp;

Introducing &ldquo;Royal Boat&rdquo;, a luxury American ship ready to sail you across the seas of Tenerife in an unbeatable fishing experience. A boat trip to enjoy fishing and nature, the sun and marine fauna. The Canary Islands are considered one of the best locations in the world thanks to the Atlantic currents, and are home to more than 5,000 marine species.

Enjoy an exciting private fishing experience with your family or friends on the &ldquo;Royal Garden Boat&rdquo;. The outing begins at the Puerto Colón pier, from where we&rsquo;ll head to the deeper waters near the coast. The Canary Islands are considered one of the best locations in the world to find large species thanks to the Atlantic currents. It&rsquo;s one of the few places where you can catch bluefin tuna, yellowfin tuna, bigeye tuna, blue marlin, white marlin, spearfish, dorado, barracuda and more.

If you prefer deep-sea fishing, the Canary Islands have excellent sea beds for this type of fishing. Here you can fish different species, such as the greater amberjack, dentex, sama, comber, blackbelly rosefish and grouper.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Discover the Teide National Park, the most visited in Europe, on this guided tour that includes tickets for the cable car ride up and down. Explore the impressive volcanic landscapes of Las Cañadas del Teide accompanied by an official guide, while you learn about its history and geological formation.&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Teide, at 3,718 metres, is the highest peak in Spain and the third highest volcano on the planet measured from the seabed. Its geological history goes back hundreds of thousands of years, with successive eruptions that have shaped the landscape of Las Cañadas del Teide, where you will find lava flows from different eras and spectacular rock formations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

From the top cable car station, you can choose between three viewpoints and trails to admire the landscape:&nbsp;
La Rambleta viewpoint - Panoramic views of Siete Cañadas and the Ucanca Valley.
Sendero de La Fortaleza - Perfect for contemplating the north of Tenerife with its forests and cliffs.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Pico Viejo Viewpoint Trail - Breathtaking views of the 800 metre diameter crater of Pico Viejo and the neighbouring islands.&nbsp;

With your booking, you will have free access to the Teide Legend digital audio guide, available in 8 languages (Spanish, English, German, French, Italian, Russian, Polish and Dutch). This audio guide will allow you to discover the history, geology and biodiversity of the National Park, as well as to learn in detail about the three trails that start from the top station of the cable car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

The excursion also includes access to the Science and Legend exhibition, located in the Teide Cable Car Visitor Centre. Through this exhibition, you will learn about the last great eruption of Teide, which occurred approximately 1,000 years ago, and how the ancient Guanches interpreted this natural phenomenon as a battle between their gods. With the audio guide, you can explore this exhibition in the language of your choice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

This collective transport tour is the best way to explore Teide in a responsible way, reducing the environmental impact and helping to conserve this World Heritage Site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Book now and live the experience of being at the top of Tenerife!

Set course for a unique island in the world and explore it comfortably in a small group aboard a Jeep Safari.

The experience includes everything: Tamaran will pick you up at your accommodation or nearby and take you to the starting point, Puerto de la Cruz for departures from the North and Playa de las Americas for those from the South. Then the ferry will take you calmly through Atlantic waters to San Sebastián de La Gomera, your first contact with an island capable of surprising both locals and strangers: did you know that it has its own language based on whistles, the &lsquo;silbo gomero&rsquo;, which is a World Heritage Site?

The caravan of jeeps that you will be part of will take you through the most fascinating parts of the island: the Hermigua Valley, the impressive Garajonay National Park, Laguna Grande or the municipality of Agulo. You will be fascinated by the friendliness of its people and the incredible natural heritage, present wherever you look.&nbsp;

This Jeep Safari in La Gomera also includes lunch in a local restaurant, where you can experience the local delicacies before heading to the end of the route, at which point the ferry will return to the starting point and you to your accommodation or nearby point. You&#39;ll do so with a smile on your face, the result of having visited one of the most unique islands in the world.&nbsp;

Embark on an exciting half-day Jeep Safari 4x4 tour of the breathtaking Teide National Park. Perfect for families, this adventure will take you through unique volcanic landscapes, such as the multicoloured crater of Pico Viejo and the iconic Roques de García.&nbsp; It&#39;s the perfect length for them to marvel at the charms and curiosities of Teide.&nbsp;

This Jeep Safari tour takes you comfortably into the less explored corners of the southern part of the island of Tenerife, where small villages like Vilaflor have had to learn to coexist on the back of a dormant volcano like Mount Teide. If you were looking for adventure, you&#39;ve found it!&nbsp; The experience starts at your accommodation (or point close to it), where the Jeep will pick you up a while before the start of the excursion. We will confirm the exact time when you make your booking. Then the route will start on the way to the National Park, declared a World Heritage Site, to show you and explain everything about such a natural temple. You will discover places such as the emblematic Roques de García or Pico Viejo.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Moto Tour Tenerife offers a unique and unforgettable experience for those who want to explore the wonderful island of Tenerife. With their&nbsp;exciting motorbike tours,&nbsp;you will have the opportunity to explore the most beautiful corners of the island without worrying about anything; the team takes care of everything so that you can enjoy the adventure to the fullest.

These guided tours are designed to&nbsp;suit the preferences and needs&nbsp;of each client. Whether you&#39;re looking for a&nbsp;leisurely ride&nbsp;through picturesque landscapes or a thrilling route along winding roads, Moto Tour Tenerife offers the flexibility to create a personalised experience.&nbsp;

Tenerife is a motorbike lover&#39;s paradise, with an impressive diversity of landscapes and roads. Enjoy hundreds of kilometres of endless curves, forest tracks and spectacular views that will make every kilometre a new adventure -&nbsp;your journey through this magical island awaits!&nbsp;

Get ready for a thrilling adventure on the Teide!

Explore these wonderful volcanic landscapes with Jurassic Quad Tenerife and feel the adrenaline as you drive through volcanic areas and lush forests. Enjoy the best views, feel the wind in your face with sea views, while you press the accelerator. In addition, during the excursion there will be stops so that you can get to know all the curiosities of El Teide and its nature.&nbsp;

Excitement is guaranteed!&nbsp;

You will be accompanied at all times by monitors who will ensure your safety throughout the excursion.&nbsp;

Ready for an experience full of excitement and spectacular scenery? Explore Tenerife in a unique way, whether it&#39;s ascending the majestic Teide National Park or touring the island&#39;s stunning coastline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Drive a modern and safe quad bike, designed for all types of terrain, from volcanic trails to coastal paths. You don&#39;t need any previous experience: the expert guides will give you all the instructions you need to get the most out of your ride.&nbsp; Feel the adrenaline rush as you pass through otherworldly landscapes, past lava flows, Canary Island pine forests and viewpoints with breathtaking views of Spain&#39;s highest volcano.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Or discover the coastline of Tenerife from a different perspective, travelling along hidden paths, cliffs and volcanic beaches with the Atlantic as a backdrop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

If you are inexperienced and are looking for an exciting and different activity in Tenerife, this is the option for you.&nbsp;

Helidream offers you a selection of quality routes to fly in helicopter, enjoy and relax with breathtaking views of the island.&nbsp;
They have a professional and highly qualified team that will make each flight a unique, special and unforgettable experience.

The best way to get to know and photograph the unique and magical landscape of Tenerife!

The Canary Islands is one of the three best spots in the world to observe the sky, along with Chile and Hawaii.

The Teide Observatory is the largest solar observatory in the world and it contains many solar and nocturnal telescopes owned by various European countries.

If you would like to make your own way to the Izaña Observatory for your guided visit, you must arrive at least 15 minutes before the tour is scheduled to start.

The Teide Observatory is located at an altitude of 2,390 m, in the area of Izaña. The entrance of the observatory is located at Km. 37 of the TF-24 highway.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Museum of Illusions contains a permanent exhibition is a 700 m2 space filled with illusions, scientific inventions and artistic expressions where physics and optics share space with mysterious works of art and classic riddles. You can enjoy a unique educational experience with interactive activities, such as light drawing or shadow making, and create unforgettable memories in our incredible upside-down world.

Do you have questions about how an invention works, do you want to hear amazing stories about art and history, do you want to expand your scientific knowledge or capture the moment with a photo? The museum team is always there for you! Its assistants are ready to reveal the secrets of the incredible world of illusions with a smile on their faces.

The permanent exhibition often undergoes small changes and new items are added to the collection every year. The museum team is constantly researching and exploring the world of science and art in search of new artistic solutions.&nbsp;

TACOA, the first Craft Brewery and Brewery-Restaurant in the Canary Islands and the oldest in Spain, offers a unique experience for craft beer lovers and those interested in the art of brewing.

During the guided tour you will be fully immersed in the process of creating these craft beers, brewed with passion and dedication. At the end of the visit, you will have the opportunity to taste four varieties of our beers. Depending on which option you choose, you can also enjoy a delicious Canarian cheese platter or lunch in TACOA&#39;s restaurant, which offers a wide variety of dishes.&nbsp;

TACOA also specialises in brewing beers for other brands, customising beers for private events and other companies. It also has a Brew Shop where you can buy bottled beers, gift packs, crown packs and suitcase packs, beer boxes of 20 units with interesting offers, and, of course, merchandising.

Don&#39;t miss the opportunity to enter the exciting world of craft beer with TACOA and live a unique sensory experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Visit the Montesdeoca Cheese Factory, where the master cheesemakers make some of the tastiest cheeses in the Canary Islands. With a great deal of effort and hard work, their cheeses and dairy products have won awards on more than 90 occasions, at island, national and international level.&nbsp;

In addition, a visit to their facilities will show you how they look after the animals, what they are fed and how they obtain the fresh milk they need to make their products.&nbsp;

A modest family farm that is firmly committed to local production, maintaining its commitment to preserving the tradition and uniqueness of artisan products made in the Canary Islands.&nbsp;

Utopia Pool Party takes place at Cielo de Monkey Beach Club in the heart of Tenerife South.

With House, RnB, Hip Hop, DnB, EDM, Reggaeton, Deep House, Tropical Bass... here you will find music and fun for all tastes.

